@startuml
title KiwiDB — State Machine: MemTable lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Active : created by\nMemTableManager

state Active {
  [*] --> Writable
  Writable --> Writable : put(key, seq, ts, value)\n[under threshold]
}
note right of Active
  Backed by a concurrent skip list.
  Accepts writes; serves reads.
end note

Active --> Frozen : threshold exceeded\n/ manual flush()\n(snapshot + new active table)

state Frozen {
  [*] --> Queued
  Queued --> Queued : served read-only\n(binary search)
}
note right of Frozen
  Immutable. Sits in the
  immutable queue (max N).
  New writes apply backpressure
  if the queue is full.
end note

Frozen --> Flushing : FlushPipeline\npicks up snapshot
Flushing --> Flushed : SSTable written + committed\n(WAL truncated, popped from queue)
Flushing --> Frozen : write failed /\nbatch aborted (retry)

Flushed --> [*]

@enduml
